  └── android.device-control
      └── configure-sandbox-routing Configure sandbox routing on an Android device without generating a test user or
setting up headless login.

Use this tool when:
- You've already logged in (manually, via deeplink, or another method)
- You want to route the app's traffic to a custom sandbox (e.g., an OnDemand server)

Prerequisites:
- A debug build of the app must be installed on the device. Release builds are not
  debuggable and cannot be configured.
- Call this AFTER login (e.g., ConfigureTestingEnvironment), not before.

After calling this tool, force-stop and relaunch the app for the routing to take effect.

Android only. For FBLite/IG Lite, a user_id is required for signed properties.

Example: To route Facebook to your OD:
  configure_sandbox_routing(device_id="emulator-5554", app_identifier="facebook",
    sandbox_hosts={"www_host": {"addr": "od123.od.facebook.com"}})  (score: 0.00793651)

